# FlopCpp - An Algebraic Modeling Language in C++

FlopCpp is an algebraic modeling language implemented as a C++ class library. It provides a high-level interface for formulating linear and mixed-integer programming problems within C++ applications. FlopCpp is part of the [COIN-OR](https://www.coin-or.org/) (Computational Infrastructure for Operations Research) initiative.

## Table of Contents

- [Features](#features)
- [Installation](#installation)
  - [Prerequisites](#prerequisites)
